  "findings": [
    "Startup flags compare the observed ~150ms and ~182ms TTFT modes; each arm has two low/eight high observations. Mode origin remains unassigned; equal sample counts are not equivalence proof or a flag waiver.",
    "Three C2 actor0 TTFT comparisons switch from the lower to higher observed mode (~63\u201370ms increase). Both modes also occur in baseline; candidate frequency differs in this sample. Causation is unresolved.",
    "Short-C2 actor1 completion-tail flags often accompany changed proposal/acceptance work and earlier whole-request completion. Per-phase regressions remain visible; end-to-end gain does not waive them.",
    "Two max-gap comparisons remain unresolved. Client and server gap fields represent two entries for each underlying request comparison.",
    "Primary C1 gain is first-pass-specific; repeated C1 is inconclusive. C2 natural adaptive-work changes limit equal-compute attribution."
  ],
